# Templates are COPY-OUT scaffolds, not packages of this repository.
#
# Each subdirectory is a self-contained workspace a user copies elsewhere, so
# several of them legitimately ship packages of the SAME name — `demo_bringup`
# appears in four, `robot_entry` in four, plus `talker_pkg`, `listener_pkg`,
# `c_talker_pkg` and `consumer` in two each. Any pkg-index walk that reaches
# this directory therefore dies on a duplicate:
#
#   nros::main!: build_pkg_index: duplicate pkg name `demo_bringup` in workspace
#   `/…/nano-ros`: `…/templates/c-and-cpp-mixed-workspace/src/demo_bringup`
#   and `…/templates/multi-node-workspace/src/demo_bringup`
#
# ONE marker here rather than one per template: the whole directory is
# scaffolding. Building a template DIRECTLY is unaffected — the walker never
# filters its own root (`depth() == 0`), which is what the `metadata_cpp`
# compile-check relies on.
